> can anyone give me some general tips on playing a tourist? I just started
> one and seem to have had abit of luck: GDSM, boots of speed, cloak of
> invisibility, magic bane, vorpal blade (I'm only on Dlvl5).  The only
> problem is this character doesn't seem to be able to destroy everything he
> comes across like barbarians can. Anyway how do I keep this character from
> dying? (aside from not doing stupid things with cockatrices)

You're already past the hardest part, you have MR and a
decent (for the early game) AC. Your tourist will fight just
as well as your barbarian if he lives long enough. Plus the
tourist artifact is a lot better than the barbarian's.

In general the best way to keep from dying is to get MR,
reflection and a low AC and then pay attention. Your AC
isn't low enough if you regularly get beat down to half your
HP. You can improve it by donating, rummaging and
enchanting.

Good luck.
